WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.472 --> 00:00:03.723
- [Narrator] Popcorn, movies, a match made

00:00:03.723 --> 00:00:05.664
in theater heaven.

00:00:05.664 --> 00:00:09.164
But there was a time when this was banned.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.928
Popcorn has been around
for over 8,000 years,

00:00:16.928 --> 00:00:19.445
but when it hit American
streets in the mid-1800s,

00:00:19.445 --> 00:00:21.045
it took off.

00:00:21.045 --> 00:00:23.477
It was cheap and could be
mass produced on the go,

00:00:23.477 --> 00:00:26.048
not to mention it smelled amazing.

00:00:26.048 --> 00:00:27.851
It was the go-to snack at circuses,

00:00:27.851 --> 00:00:29.557
sporting events and fairs.

00:00:29.557 --> 00:00:32.117
In fact the only place
you wouldn't find popcorn

00:00:32.117 --> 00:00:33.617
was at the movies.

00:00:34.581 --> 00:00:36.555
You see, going to the movies used to be

00:00:36.555 --> 00:00:38.496
a major event.

00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:40.736
The only people that went
were fancy rich folks

00:00:40.736 --> 00:00:43.189
because you had to be
educated enough to read.

00:00:43.189 --> 00:00:46.389
Fancy, like there was even a coat check.

00:00:46.389 --> 00:00:48.832
But there was definitely
no concession stand.

00:00:48.832 --> 00:00:50.997
There was, however, popcorn street vendors

00:00:50.997 --> 00:00:52.928
who set up shop outside theaters.

00:00:52.928 --> 00:00:55.776
They made a killing selling
to waiting theater goers.

00:00:55.776 --> 00:00:57.201
Theater goers that started smuggling

00:00:57.201 --> 00:00:58.886
their popped treats inside.

00:00:58.886 --> 00:01:00.134
Not cool.

00:01:00.134 --> 00:01:02.278
Early movie theaters kindly asked patrons

00:01:02.278 --> 00:01:04.380
check their popcorn before entering.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:07.633
Then, in 1927, films started adding sound,

00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:09.713
meaning everyone went to the movies.

00:01:09.713 --> 00:01:11.548
The Great Depression
followed making movies

00:01:11.548 --> 00:01:12.785
a cheap escape.

00:01:12.785 --> 00:01:15.398
Huge crowds plus crunch
muffling sound equaled

00:01:15.398 --> 00:01:18.310
another revenue opportunity
for theater owners.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:21.244
By 1945, over half the popcorn consumed

00:01:21.244 --> 00:01:24.006
in America was being eaten at the movies.

00:01:24.006 --> 00:01:26.268
A marriage that has continued ever since.

00:01:26.268 --> 00:01:29.851
♫ To get ourselves a treat

